{"name":"Light Cipollino","hex":"#d5dad1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"cipollino","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of cipolin (“type of marble”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cipollino"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cipollino","blocks":[{"text":"Cipollino, or Little Onion as translated from the original, is a fictional character from Gianni Rodari's eponymous Tale of Cipollino written in 1951. Also known under its 1957 renamed title Adventures of Cipollino, it is a children's tale about political oppression. He also appeared before the publication of the book in the children's magazine Il Pioniere of which Rodari was the editor. Cipollino was popular in the Soviet Union, up to the point of being adapted as a ballet composed by Karen Khachaturian and choreographed by Henrich Mayorov, originally staged in Taras Shevchenko National Opera and Ballet Theatre of Ukraine on November 8, 1974."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Russia_stamp_1992_No_16.jpg/330px-Russia_stamp_1992_No_16.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cipollino","wikidata":"Q4516121"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG/500px-Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG/1280px-Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG/500px-Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Beam of sun light inside the cavity of Rocca ill'Abissu at Fondachelli-Fantina, Sicily","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARocca_dell'Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Optical_refraction_at_water_surface.jpg/500px-Optical_refraction_at_water_surface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Optical_refraction_at_water_surface.jpg/500px-Optical_refraction_at_water_surface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Due to refraction, the straw dipped in water appears bent and the ruler scale compressed when viewed from a shallow angle.","link":"https://en.